{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A world holds data: entities and their components, and resources. A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"system"}]},{"type":"text","text":" holds a rule: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"step that reads part of the world and changes part of it, such as “every entity with a velocity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moves” or “gravity pulls on everything that isn’t frozen.” A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"schedule"}]},{"type":"text","text":" lists the systems of one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frame or step and runs them on a world, each once per run."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and event:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double, y: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double, dy: Double }","struct Health: Component { var current: Int }","struct Frozen: Component {}","","struct Score: Resource { var points: Int }","struct TimeStep: Resource { var seconds: Double }","struct Paused: Resource {}","","struct Damage: Event { var target: Entity, amount: Int }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Declare a System","anchor":"Declare-a-System","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The simplest way to write a system is to mark a type with the "},{"code":"@System","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro and give it a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method. The method’s parameters say what the system works on, and their types say how:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update"},{"type":"text","text":" writes components, a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them, and a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads a resource. The following two systems pull everything that isn’t frozen downward, then move"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it by its velocity:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@System","struct Gravity {","    func run(_ falling: Update<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        falling { velocity, _ in velocity.dy -= 10 }","    }","}","","@System","struct Movement {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","            position.y += row.components.dy","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because the parameters’ types state what each system reads and writes, the macro writes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for you: "},{"code":"Gravity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"Movement","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads "},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A schedule uses the access to decide which systems can run at the same time."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also conform a type to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" by hand and write its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" method, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"receives the whole world. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for when to do that.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Run Systems in a Schedule","anchor":"Run-Systems-in-a-Schedule","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","type":"reference"},{"text":" is built from a list of systems, written in a result builder. Running it runs each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system once. The following example drops a ball for one frame:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 90.0)\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems run in the order you write them, unless an ordering constraint says otherwise.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"after(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"before(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" require one system to run after or before another; ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names a group of systems so constraints can refer to all of them at once; and ","type":"text"},{"code":"runIf(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" skips","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a system when a condition doesn’t hold.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems whose accesses don’t conflict, because neither writes what the other reads or writes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run at the same time, and the world ends as though they had run one after another (commands","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apply when each wave finishes). Systems that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conflict run in order. When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, their order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rests only on how they happen to be written; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" finds those pairs so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"test can keep a schedule free of them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"metadata":{"externalID":"Systems","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","title":"Systems","roleHeading":"Framework"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"]},{"title":"System Parameters","anchor":"System-Parameters","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents"]},{"title":"Building and Running Schedules","anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"]},{"title":"Main-Actor Systems","anchor":"Main-Actor-Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"]},{"title":"Built-In Systems","anchor":"Built-In-Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges"]},{"title":"Profiling","anchor":"Profiling","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming"]}],"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/run(in:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"run"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"World"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","title":"run(in:)","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/run(in:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs the system’s rule once on a world."}],"required":true},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/CyclicOrdering":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/cyclicordering","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An error indicating that the ordering constraints of a schedule’s systems form a cycle, so no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order satisfies them all."}],"title":"CyclicOrdering","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CyclicOrdering"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CyclicOrdering"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Ambiguity":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Ambiguity","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/ambiguity","type":"topic","title":"Ambiguity","abstract":[{"text":"Two systems of a schedule whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint orders, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the order they run in rests only on the order they were written in.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Ambiguity","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run.","type":"text"}],"title":"SystemProfile","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemProfile"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemProfile"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventReader":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","title":"EventReader","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventreader","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that reads the events of one type sent since the system last read them.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardChanges":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ForwardChanges","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges","title":"ForwardChanges","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ForwardChanges","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardchanges","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that yields each component of one type added or changed since it last ran to an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asynchronous stream, with its entity."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemTiming":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemTiming"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming","kind":"symbol","title":"SystemTiming","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemTiming"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemtiming","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The times one system of a schedule has taken to run.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/UpdateEvents":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UpdateEvents"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A system that ends the current event update, dropping events old enough that every reader","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has had its chance to read them.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","title":"UpdateEvents","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/updateevents","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UpdateEvents"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/MainActorSystem":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainActorSystem"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem","title":"MainActorSystem","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/mainactorsystem","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainActorSystem"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A system that runs on the main actor, for work that touches main-actor state such as a user","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interface.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/access":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"access","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Access","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6AccessV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","title":"access","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/access","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The component, resource and event types the system reads and writes, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" if it may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change anything."}],"defaultImplementations":1,"required":true},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemSet":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemSet"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","kind":"symbol","title":"SystemSet","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemSet"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemset","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that names a group of systems, so ordering constraints can refer to all of them at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Query":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A description of the entities to visit and the components to read from each.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","type":"topic","title":"Query","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/query","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceWriter":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceWriter"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads and writes a resource."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","title":"ResourceWriter","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcewriter","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceWriter"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DeclaringSystems":{"role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/declaringsystems","type":"topic","title":"Declaring Systems","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write the rules of a simulation as systems, and let their parameters state what they read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","kind":"article"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardEvents":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ForwardEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardevents","type":"topic","title":"ForwardEvents","abstract":[{"text":"A system that yields each event of one type to an asynchronous stream, so code outside the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule can await the events.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ForwardEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduleBuilder":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduleBuilder"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A result builder that collects the systems written in a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"’s closure."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","title":"ScheduleBuilder","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulebuilder","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduleBuilder"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp":{"abstract":[{"text":"Hold a world in your app or game engine, feed it each frame’s input, and let the objects outside","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it read results and take part in a step.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","title":"Driving a World from an App","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/drivingaworldfromanapp","kind":"article"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/RemovedComponents":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RemovedComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents","kind":"symbol","title":"RemovedComponents","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RemovedComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/removedcomponents","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that lists the entities that lost a component since the system last read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/ambiguities()":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ambiguities"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"text":"Ambiguity","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Returns every pair of systems whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"orders.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","type":"topic","title":"ambiguities()","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguities()","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","title":"Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"role":"collection"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System()":{"fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Makes a type a system whose access comes from the parameters of its ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","title":"System()","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system()","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Update":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Update","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that changes a component of every entity that holds it."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","title":"Update","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/update","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Update","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A rule that reads and changes a world, run once each time its schedule runs.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","type":"topic","title":"System","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","type":"topic","title":"Schedule","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemParameter":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemParameter","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemparameter","title":"SystemParameter","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemParameter","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type a system’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method can take in place of the whole world, whose type states what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the system reads and writes."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduledSystem":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduledSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","title":"ScheduledSystem","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScheduledSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/scheduledsystem","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system together with the ordering constraints, sets and conditions a schedule runs it with."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventWriter":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventWriter"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","kind":"symbol","title":"EventWriter","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventWriter"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventwriter","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that sends events of one type."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceReader":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceReader"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","kind":"symbol","title":"ResourceReader","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceReader"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcereader","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads a resource."}]}}}